  "findings": [
    "Finite eventually_all over both parent edge indices obtains a single neighborhood. Crossing is an implication, so noncrossing pairs add no premise. Every crossing has both strict parameter inequalities, nonzero ordered determinant, its unchanged sign and actual child crossing.",
    "The inherited crossing support is the deterministic Finset image of the parent pair. Subtype equality uses equality of those supports. The canonical point identity follows from the frozen supporting-point/crossingPoint theorem with child G1.",
    "The two visits select each member of the same unordered support, reversing only the pair representation. The canonical parameter identity uses softInheritedVisit_parameter and its actual edge label, not a chosen unrelated parameter.",
    "All three limits use global supporting-line functions at zero with nonzero parent crossing determinant. Both parameter limits are rewritten to the actual parent pairVisit parameters. No G1 or Generic hypothesis is imposed on the duplicate-vertex tuple at zero.",
    "The positive-radius theorem intersects finite persistence with the source-derived Generic/transport radius. The distance conversion uses positivity of epsilon. It concludes child Generic and persistence from hn3, parent Generic and SoftAdmissible, then supplies the canonical identities on that same interval.",
    "Root observed first92045 terminal exit0. Six standard-only axiom traces, 16 ordered full-body embeddings, 15 predecessor body receipts and first-draft byte equality verified."
  ],
